  "body": "**Stacked on #478** (#383, the Machines pane edits and saves `.mch` files). The #480 work is a95093c0.\n\n## What changed\nA `.mch` saved from the Machines pane keeps the key order it was read in. Keys the file didn't have go at the end of their object. Project files are untouched.\n\n- **New `crates/app/src/machine/order.rs`** (with provenance).\n  - It reads the source text once and records the key order of every object and array as a `KeyOrder` tree. A duplicated key keeps its first position and takes its last value, like `serde_json::Value`.\n  - `to_pretty(value, order)` writes the same layout as `to_string_pretty` (2-space indent, `\": \"`), with keys in the recorded order, then any unknown keys sorted.\n- **`MachineDraft`** gains `order: KeyOrder`. `open` and `from_template` fill it from the source, `blank` leaves it empty, and `text()` writes through `to_pretty`. Edits still act on the plain `serde_json::Value`, so `fields.rs` is unchanged.\n- **No new dependency, and `serde_json/preserve_order` is not turned on workspace-wide.** That would change every JSON writer, project files included. `indexmap` is already in the lock file, but using it directly would still be a dependency change, and the order visitor is about 60 lines.\n- The `docs/decisions/383-machines-edit.md` \"key order\" entry is replaced by this decision.\n\n## How tested\n- `machine_edit::a_saved_file_keeps_its_key_order_and_new_keys_go_last`: a hand-written file in deliberately unsorted order, with unknown keys, gets an edit plus a new `spindle`/`max_speed` block. The saved file's exact key list is checked.\n- `machine_edit::a_new_machine_writes_the_same_text_serde_json_would`: with no recorded order, the output matches `to_string_pretty` byte for byte.\n- `machine_edit`, `machine_library`, `machine` and `project_roundtrip` (69) pass. Project files are byte-identical; no project writer changed.\n- `clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Limitation\nOnly the key order is kept. A hand-written file's inline arrays (e.g. `[0, 0, 1]` on one line) still come out multi-line.\n\nChangelog: A machine file saved from the Machines pane keeps its key order (new keys go last) (#480)\n\nFixes #480\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
